// BT-4721: a REPL redefinition (`X >> m => ...`) of a method that the loaded
// file defines replaces it, and the class source the workspace stores stays
// canonical: a later `compile:source:` (the IDE/MCP save path) of another
// selector still compiles. A stored source that kept both the body method and
// the appended extension would be a duplicate-method error there.
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/same_file_redefine.bt

SameFileRedefine new foo
// => 1

SameFileRedefine >> foo => 2
// => "SameFileRedefine>>foo"

SameFileRedefine new foo
// => 2

SameFileRedefine compile: #bar source: "bar => 20"
// => SameFileRedefine

SameFileRedefine new bar
// => 20

// The earlier redefinition survived the second save.
SameFileRedefine new foo
// => 2
